":\\\"u10\\\"},\\n    {\\\"reason\\\":\\\"Practicability qualifies SFC operational improvements, not the filing duty; case-officer contact is enquiry guidance.\\\",\\\"status\\\":\\\"INTERPRETED\\\",\\\"unit_id\\\":\\\"u11\\\"},\\n    {\\\"reason\\\":\\\"Identifies the issuing division.\\\",\\\"status\\\":\\\"CONTEXT\\\",\\\"unit_id\\\":\\\"u12\\\"},\\n    {\\\"reason\\\":\\\"Identifies the issuing regulator.\\\",\\\"status\\\":\\\"CONTEXT\\\",\\\"unit_id\\\":\\\"u13\\\"},\\n    {\\\"reason\\\":\\\"End marker has no substantive effect.\\\",\\\"status\\\":\\\"CONTEXT\\\",\\\"unit_id\\\":\\\"u14\\\"},\\n    {\\\"reason\\\":\\\"Identifies product categories relevant to the coverage determination.\\\",\\\"status\\\":\\\"INTERPRETED\\\",\\\"unit_id\\\":\\\"u17\\\"},\\n    {\\\"reason\\\":\\\"Expands WINGS; creates no additional condition or exception.\\\",\\\"status\\\":\\\"CONTEXT\\\",\\\"unit_id\\\":\\\"u18\\\"}\\n  ],\\n  \\\"dimensions\\\": [\\n    {\\\"dimension\\\":\\\"scope\\\",\\\"explanation\\\":\\\"The control concerns persons making covered applications or submissions to IPD, including the reporting requests identified in u9. It is not a whole-institution compliance test or a duty imposed on every e-IP user merely by user status.\\\",\\\"source_unit_ids\\\":[\\\"u1\\\",\\\"u3\\\",\\\"u9\\\",\\\"u17\\\"],\\\"status\\\":\\\"PROPOSED\\\"},\\n    {\\\"dimension\\\":\\\"definitions\\\",\\\"explanation\\\":\\\"IPD and SFC are identified in the text; footnote 1 supplies product categories and footnote 2 expands WINGS. Treating the product list as exhaustive remains an explicit assumption rather than a separately established definition.\\\",\\\"source_unit_ids\\\":[\\\"u1\\\",\\\"u12\\\",\\\"u13\\\",\\\"u17\\\",\\\"u18\\\"],\\\"status\\\":\\\"PROPOSED\\\"},\\n    {\\\"dimension\\\":\\\"exceptions\\\",\\\"explanation\\\":\\\"Existing-channel acceptance attaches to the parallel run as extended. Neither planned enhancements nor 'where practicable' supplies an exception to post-transition filing. No express grandfathering provision appears.\\\",\\\"source_unit_ids\\\":[\\\"u4\\\",\\\"u7\\\",\\\"u9\\\",\\\"u11\\\"],\\\"status\\\":\\\"PROPOSED\\\"},\\n    {\\\"dimension\\\":\\\"modality\\\",\\\"explanation\\\":\\\"'Must' governs filing routes; 'can also' permits annual-fee settlement. The SFC's statements about integration and improvements do not make the filing duty conditional on completed enhancements.\\\",\\\"source_unit_ids\\\":[\\\"u7\\\",\\\"u9\\\",\\\"u11\\\"],\\\"status\\\":\\\"PROPOSED\\\"},\\n    {\\\"dimension\\\":\\\"time\\\",\\\"explanation\\\":\\\"The extension ends on 29 November 2024 and compulsory use begins on 30 November 2024. The text does not specify which event dates a filing spanning the transition.\\\",\\\"source_unit_ids\\\":[\\\"u1\\\",\\\"u3\\\",\\\"u4\\\",\\\"u7\\\",\\\"u9\\\"],\\\"status\\\":\\\"AMBIGUOUS\\\"},\\n    {\\\"dimension\\\":\\\"dependencies\\\",\\\"explanation\\\":\\\"The earlier circular is referenced but unavailable, and external-authorities.24ec50 is reported missing. Its contents cannot establish additional exceptions, channel definitions, or transitional treatment here.\\\",\\\"source_unit_ids\\\":[\\\"u3\\\",\\\"u4\\\",\\\"u9\\\"],\\\"status\\\":\\\"AMBIGUOUS\\\"}\\n  ],\\n  \\\"questions\\\": [\\n    \\\"How is the relevant filing date determined for an application initiated before 30 November 2024 but completed or supplemented afterward?\\\",\\n    \\\"Does the unavailable 8 July 2024 circular or other missing authority specify grandfathering, operational exceptions, or the meaning of existing channels?\\\",\\n    \\\"Is footnote 1 intended to exhaustively delimit covered products?\\\"\\n  ],\\n  \\\"readings\\\": [\\n    {\\n      \\\"assumptions\\\": [\\n        \\\"The product categories in footnote 1 delimit the covered products, subject also to IPD administration.\\\",\\n        \\\"Extending the parallel run preserves its existing-channel acceptance throughout the extension.\\\",\\n        \\\"The transition uses Hong Kong calendar dates without an inferred time-of-day rule.\\\",\\n        \\\"The filing-date fact is supplied only once the relevant filing event is established; unresolved transitional cases remain unknown.\\\"\\n      ],\\n      \\\"citations\\\": [\\n        {\\\"quote\\\":\\\"During this period, the SFC continues to accept applications and submissions via existing channels.\\\",\\\"unit_id\\\":\\\"u4\\\"},\\n        {\\\"quote\\\":\\\"To facilitate these enhancements, the SFC will extend the parallel run period of e-IP by one month to 29 November 2024.\\\",\\\"unit_id\\\":\\\"u7\\\"},\\n        {\\\"quote\\\":\\\"Starting 30 November 2024, ie, after the parallel run period, applications and submissions of investment products administered by IPD must be submitted via e-IP.\\\",\\\"unit_id\\\":\\\"u9\\\"},\\n        {\\\"quote\\\":\\\"The current submission requests from IPD via the IP E-submission system will be integrated into e-IP, including reporting of net asset values, large redemptions and suspensions of dealing.\\\",\\\"unit_id\\\":\\\"u9\\\"},\\n        {\\\"quote\\\":\\\"In addition, e-IP users can also settle recurring annual fees associated with relevant investment products through the new system.\\\",\\\"unit_id\\\":\\\"u9\\\"},\\n        {\\\"quote\\\":\\\"The SFC will continue to review and enhance the operation of e-IP where practicable.\\\",\\\"unit_id\\\":\\\"u11\\\"},\\n        {\\\"quote\\\":\\\"1 Investment-linked assurance schemes, mandatory provident fund products, open-ended fund companies, paper gold schemes, pooled retirement funds, real estate investment trusts, unit trusts and mutual funds and unlisted structured investment products.\\\",\\\"unit_id\\\":\\\"u17\\\"}\\n      ],\\n      \\\"distinction\\\":\\\"The existing-channel permission is a temporary allowance carried forward by the extension. The hypothesis that 'where practicable' excuses users from mandatory e-IP filing fails because that qualifier attaches to the SFC's review and enhancement activity. An enhancement-completion condition likewise lacks textual support. Attaching 'During this period' exclusively to the original October endpoint ignores the express extension of that same parallel run. No materially supported rival exception is retained; the strongest uncertainty is treatment of filings spanning the transition.\\\",\\n      \\\"family\\\":\\\"exceptions\\\",\\n      \\\"formalization\\\":{\\n        \\\"facts\\\":[\\n          {\\\"meaning\\\":\\\"The selected filing is an application or submission of an investment product administered by IPD.\\\",\\\"name\\\":\\\"covered_ipd_filing\\\",\\\"requires_judgment\\\":true,\\\"source_unit_ids\\\":[\\\"u1\\\",\\\"u9\\\",\\\"u17\\\"],\\\"type\\\":\\\"bool\\\",\\\"unit\\\":\\\"Boolean\\\"},\\n          {\\\"meaning\\\":\\\"The filing date is on or after the compulsory transition date.\\\",\\\"name\\\":\\\"filing_on_or_after_2024_11_30\\\",\\\"requires_judgment\\\":false,\\\"source_unit_ids\\\":[\\\"u1\\\",\\\"u9\\\"],\\\"type\\\":\\\"bool\\\",\\\"unit\\\":\\\"Boolean\\\"},\\n          {\\\"meaning\\\":\\\"The covered filing was submitted through e-IP.\\\",\\\"name\\\":\\\"submitted_via_e_ip\\\",\\\"requires_judgment\\\":true,\\\"source_unit_ids\\\":[\\\"u1\\\",\\\"u9\\\"],\\\"type\\\":\\\"bool\\\",\\\"unit\\\":\\\"Boolean\\\"}\\n        ],\\n        \\\"result\\\":\\\"submitted_via_e_ip\\\",\\n        \\\"result_type\\\":\\\"bool\\\",\\n        \\\"scope\\\":\\\"(and covered_ipd_filing filing_on_or_after_2024_11_30)\\\"\\n      },\\n      \\\"local_id\\\":\\\"r1_refined\\\",\\n      \\\"questions\\\":[\\n        \\\"Which event determines the filing date for a pending application, amendment, or supplementary submission?\\\",\\n        \\\"Do unavailable referenced materials expressly preserve any existing-channel route after the transition?\\\"\\n      ],\\n      \\\"statement\\\":\\\"For the selected compulsory e-IP submission-route control, exi